tps://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113233","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113233","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113233.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113233.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-13T13:45:35Z"},"body":"Very minor core improvement with a few benefits:\r\n\r\n- Using `constexpr` means the values can be used in a `constexpr` context. This came up a few times in PRs, although none of the PRs that needed this were merged yet.\r\n- This guarantees that compilers can inline use of the value. If it isn't inlined, fetching the value can incur a cache miss cost, which is relatively expensive. \r\n    - Note that I would expect an optimizing compiler to inline the use anyway, but it's not guaranteed with `static const`.\r\n\r\nI'm convinced that this will be needed sooner or later, but since this change should be risk-free, I think it makes sense to bring it in already, to enable future PRs to use it (without big diffs).","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com